From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:08:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE on every DisplayPort
 connector, and amdgpu.dvbridge_dce on them

DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE says what passive DisplayPort dual-mode (DP++) adaptor is
behind a DisplayPort connector (none, an adaptor that says HDMI, another
one). It was attached only where the Dolby Vision tunnel is offered: on DCE
11.2 to 12 only with amdgpu.dvbridge_dce=1, and never on DCE 11.0 and
earlier. But what is behind the connector matters there too:

- a display that takes HDMI 3D gets no 3D mode on a DisplayPort connector
  without an adaptor that says HDMI (amdgpu_dm_stereo_layout(), stereo_allowed),
  and user space could only say "the display has no 3D mode for it" where the
  cause is an active converter (issue 26 of LibreELEC Hades, an A10-8730B,
  DCE 11.0, through an active DisplayPort to HDMI converter);
- through a passive adaptor, the driver takes the deepest colour that the
  display declares and the adaptor's TMDS clock carries (12 bpc for 1080p60
  through a 300 MHz adaptor to a display with 36-bit deep colour), which the
  same issue's first adaptor did not show; user space sets 8 bpc for SDR there
  as Windows and i915 send it, and needs to know the adaptor for that;
- the tunnel goes through a passive adaptor that says HDMI
  (amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_check_connector()), but the setting that turns it on on
  DCE (amdgpu.dvbridge_dce, named in HADES_BOOT_OPTION) was offered on HDMI
  connectors only, so a Polaris or Vega card on DP++ could not have it but by
  hand.

So DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE is attached to every DisplayPort connector of a single
stream, whatever the display core, and HADES_BOOT_OPTION names
amdgpu.dvbridge_dce on the DisplayPort connectors of DCE 11.2 to 12 too; user
space offers that option on a DisplayPort connector only while
DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE says "HDMI adaptor". The property is read only and was
already written each time the display is looked at (amdgpu_dm_update_dual_mode());
nothing that goes out changes.
---
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 45 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 4b1525ce9..f5afdf1ae 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -5488,8 +5488,14 @@ void amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 		drm_connector_attach_content_type_property(&aconnector->base);
 	}
 
-	if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA && amdgpu_dm_dvbridge &&
-	    adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dv_standard_property && adev->dm.dc &&
+	/*
+	 * (Hades: an HDMI connector, and a DisplayPort one (SST): the tunnel goes there through a
+	 * passive dual-mode adaptor that says HDMI, amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_check_connector(), and user
+	 * space offers the option on it only behind such an adaptor, DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE)
+	 */
+	if ((connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA ||
+	     (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort && !aconnector->mst_root)) &&
+	    amdgpu_dm_dvbridge && adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dv_standard_property && adev->dm.dc &&
 	    amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce_core(adev->dm.dc->ctx->dce_version)) {
 		const struct drm_prop_enum_list option = { 0, "amdgpu.dvbridge_dce" };
 		struct drm_property *prop;
@@ -5507,7 +5513,7 @@ void amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 		if (prop) {
 			drm_object_attach_property(&aconnector->base.base, prop, 0);
 			drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
-				      "DVBRIDGE: HADES_BOOT_OPTION amdgpu.dvbridge_dce on the HDMI connectors of this display core (now %s)\n",
+				      "DVBRIDGE: HADES_BOOT_OPTION amdgpu.dvbridge_dce on the HDMI and DisplayPort connectors of this display core (now %s)\n",
 				      amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce ? "on" : "off");
 		}
 	}
@@ -5544,20 +5550,29 @@ void amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 			drm_object_attach_property(&aconnector->base.base,
 						   adev->mode_info.dvbridge_hdr10t_property, 0);
 		/*
-		 * Hades: a DisplayPort connector says what passive adaptor is behind it
-		 * (DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE, amdgpu_dm_update_dual_mode()), and why the tunnel is refused
-		 * (DVBRIDGE_REFUSED; the HDR10 depth guard is for HDMI connectors)
+		 * Hades: a DisplayPort connector says why the tunnel is refused (DVBRIDGE_REFUSED; the
+		 * HDR10 depth guard is for HDMI connectors); what passive adaptor is behind it,
+		 * below, it says on every display core
 		 */
-		if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort) {
-			if (adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property) {
-				drm_object_attach_property(&aconnector->base.base,
-							   adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property,
-							   AMDGPU_DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE_NONE);
-				aconnector->dvbridge_dual_mode_property =
-					adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property;
-			}
+		if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort)
 			amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_attach_refused(aconnector);
-		}
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Hades: a DisplayPort connector (SST) says what passive adaptor is behind it
+	 * (DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE, amdgpu_dm_update_dual_mode()) on every display core, whether the tunnel
+	 * is offered there or not: it is also what user space needs for the depth of the link through
+	 * such an adaptor, for why a display that takes 3D gets no 3D mode on it, and for offering
+	 * amdgpu.dvbridge_dce (HADES_BOOT_OPTION) only behind an adaptor that says HDMI. Read only,
+	 * written each time the display is looked at.
+	 */
+	if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort && !aconnector->mst_root &&
+	    adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property) {
+		drm_object_attach_property(&aconnector->base.base,
+					   adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property,
+					   AMDGPU_DVBRIDGE_DUAL_MODE_NONE);
+		aconnector->dvbridge_dual_mode_property =
+			adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dual_mode_property;
 	}
 
 	/* Hades: the HDR10 depth guard and DVBRIDGE_REFUSED, on every HDMI connector */
-- 
2.53.0

